The function is used by the NFS server daemon to pass information
into  and  out  of  the  kernel and also to enter the kernel as a
server daemon.  The argument consists of several bits  that  show
what  action  is to be taken once in the kernel and the points to
any corresponding data that the action may  require.   is  called
with  the  flag and a NULL to enter the kernel as an daemon.  The
action normally does not return until the NFS server is  stopped.
The  server  daemon calls with the flag and a pointer to a struct
